{%- doc -%}
  The Tastes Like / Roast info row the 2026 theme migration dropped from individual Brew Guides
  blog articles. A block inside the existing main-blog-post section (templates/article.json),
  placed in its block_order right after the title block -- matching
  sections/article-template.liquid in Shopify theme 147471433919 ("ONA - OLD 11/26/2025"), the
  last pre-cutover snapshot, where this info sat directly under the heading, above the featured
  image and article body.

  Split out of sections/brewguide-article-info.liquid (which still carries the brew recipe and
  the cross-sell, both in their own sibling section placed after the article body) and, on a
  second round, out of being its own sibling section entirely: Codex on PR #282 first caught
  that bundling all three pieces into one section placed after main-blog-post put the tasting
  info below the full article body instead of near the title; the fix after that (a second
  sibling section placed BEFORE main-blog-post) put it above the article's own <h1> instead,
  since main-blog-post's title is the first block INSIDE that section, not before it. A block
  nested inside main-blog-post's own block_order is the only way to land between the title and
  the rest of the post -- main-blog-post's schema declares "@theme" and "@app" block slots
  alongside its private _blog-post-* ones, so a custom theme block is accepted there.

  No `.section` wrapper here (unlike the sibling recipe/cross-sell section): this renders inside
  main-blog-post's own page-width wrapper already, as a sibling of the title/date/image/content
  blocks, so wrapping it in a second nested .section would double up the grid.

  Scoped to the Brew Guides blog only (article.blog.handle == 'brewguides') so it stays inert on
  News/Journal/other blogs that share templates/article.json.

  Metafield types, see reference_shopify_json_string_metafield_no_value:
    - accentuate.tastes_like   string   -> no .value, read directly
    - accentuate.roast         string   -> no .value, read directly
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign is_brewguide_article = false
  if article.blog.handle == 'brewguides'
    assign is_brewguide_article = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if is_brewguide_article -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign tastes_like = article.metafields.accentuate.tastes_like
    assign roast = article.metafields.accentuate.roast

    assign has_info = false
    if tastes_like != blank or roast != blank
      assign has_info = true
    endif
  -%}

  {%- if has_info -%}
    <dl class="brewguide-article-info" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
      {%- if tastes_like != blank -%}
        <div class="brewguide-article-info__row">
          <dt class="brewguide-article-info__label">Tastes like</dt>
          <dd class="brewguide-article-info__value">{{ tastes_like }}</dd>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if roast != blank -%}
        <div class="brewguide-article-info__row">
          <dt class="brewguide-article-info__label">Roast</dt>
          <dd class="brewguide-article-info__value">{{ roast }}</dd>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </dl>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .brewguide-article-info {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--gap-sm);
    width: 100%;
  }

  .brewguide-article-info__row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--gap-sm);
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .brewguide-article-info__label {
    font-size: var(--font-h6--size);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .brewguide-article-info__value {
    margin: 0;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Brew guide tasting info",
  "tag": null,
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Brew guide tasting info"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
